# Copy to .env and fill in.
#
# LOCAL DEV uses SQLite automatically (no setup, works offline). The default
# below is all you need locally.
DATABASE_URL="file:./dev.db"
PORT=4000
CORS_ORIGIN="http://localhost:5173"

# --- Accounts system ---------------------------------------------------------
# Sign the JWT sessions. Set a long random value in production.
JWT_SECRET="change-me-to-a-long-random-string"

# Email — verification codes, password reset, and QTN workflow notifications.
#
# ALL THREE of SMTP_HOST, SMTP_USER and SMTP_PASS are required. With any of them
# missing, mail is DISABLED: in dev the codes are logged to the console and echoed
# by the API so the flow stays testable, and in PRODUCTION sending now throws a
# visible error instead of silently reporting success.
#
# Every value here is read at MODULE LOAD, so changing one needs a server restart
# (locally) or a redeploy (Vercel). Saving the file is not enough.
#
# Google Workspace (needs 2-Step Verification on, then an App Password —
# https://myaccount.google.com/apppasswords — NOT the account password):
#   SMTP_HOST="smtp.gmail.com"
#   SMTP_PORT="587"
#   SMTP_SECURE="false"          # exact string "true" enables implicit TLS; port 465 needs BOTH
#   SMTP_USER="verification@powerline.com.eg"
#   SMTP_PASS="16-char app password"
#   SMTP_FROM="PowerLine <verification@powerline.com.eg>"
#
# Verify credentials without going through the UI:
#   node scripts/test-smtp.js                  # connect + log in only
#   node scripts/test-smtp.js you@example.com  # also send one real message

# Absolute base URL used for links inside notification e-mails (a relative path
# is useless in an inbox). Falls back to CORS_ORIGIN.
APP_URL="http://localhost:5173"

# --- Production (Vercel) only -------------------------------------------------
# On Vercel the datasource auto-switches to PostgreSQL (Neon) and tables are
# created on deploy. Set these as Environment Variables in the Vercel dashboard
# (NOT in this file):
#   DATABASE_URL = Neon POOLED url   (host contains "-pooler")
#   DIRECT_URL   = Neon DIRECT url   (no "-pooler")
